 a rule to spaced comments been talked about? I am currently linting a large code base, a large percentage of our comments do not have a space.\n\nIt seems like a pretty straight forward fix to implement, the only areas that start to get interesting are around markers and exceptions. I'm curious if this is something that might be considered for a PR though.\n\nI have currently just pulled out the spaced commented rule and made a custom version of it which I use for linting now instead of the built in and this has worked fairly well for me as our comments are simple and I don't have exceptions or markers.\n\nJust curious if this is something that might make it's way into ESLint.\n\nThanks!\n","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/eslint/eslint/issues/4969/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"timeline_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/eslint/eslint/issues/4969/timeline","performed_via_github_app":null,"state_reason":"completed"}},"event":"cross-referenced"},{"actor":{"login":"zandaqo","id":8959662,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjg5NTk2NjI=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/8959662?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/zandaqo","html_url":"https://github.com/zandaqo","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zandaqo/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zandaqo/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zandaqo/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zandaqo/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zandaqo/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zandaqo/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zandaqo/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zandaqo/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zandaqo/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2016-